<OmiItchNasdaqEquitiesPdf>

  <!-- NtxEquities MatchView 1.10 -->

  <!-- Transcribed from NTXMatchView_v1_1.pdf, Nasdaq Texas MatchView (formerly known as Ouch Pricing
       Feed) Version 1.10; revision history to "Version 1.0 - 2/13/2026: Name change to Nasdaq Texas"
       (the earlier entries: 1.0 12/15/2008 publication, 1.1 1/26/2010 symbol widened from 6 to 8
       characters, 1.1 8/10/2011 feed renamed). The layout is the BX MatchView 1.10 layout
       (BxEquities/MatchView/BXMatchView_v1 1.pdf) under the Nasdaq Texas name.

       MatchView gives the view the Nasdaq Texas execution system has of the prevailing best bid and
       offer of the other exchanges, for use with OUCH to prevent trade-throughs and quote-throughs.

       Every field is ASCII. The one message line opens with an 8 character Time Stamp at offset 0,
       milliseconds past midnight, then the 1 character Type at offset 8, so the message header is
       Time Stamp then Message Type (as in TotalView-ITCH 2.0) and the fields below follow at offset 9.
       Prices are 10 characters, 6 whole number places followed by 4 implied decimal digits, padded with
       spaces on the left. The only message type is "U". Message length 37.

       The specification states no transport. The Nasdaq UDP/IP address pages list MatchView as a
       single channel UDP multicast broadcast, and the feed dates from 2008, so the reference frames it
       with the timestamped MoldUDP (32) packet the TotalView-ITCH 2.0 transcription uses. -->

  <Messages>

    <Message>
      <Name>Quote Update Message</Name>
      <Dependency>messagetype</Dependency>
      <Branch>payload</Branch>
      <Code>U</Code>
      <Description>The prevailing best bid and offer of the other exchanges as the Nasdaq Texas execution system sees it.</Description>
      <Fields>
        <Field>
          <Name>Stock</Name>
          <Type>Alpha</Type>
          <Size>8</Size>
          <Description>The Stock Symbol</Description>
        </Field>
        <Field>
          <Name>Bid Price</Name>
          <Type>Price (4)</Type>
          <Size>10</Size>
          <Description>The price on the bid with 6 whole number places followed by 4 decimal digits. The decimal point is implied by position; it does not appear inside the price field. The price is padded with spaces on the left.</Description>
        </Field>
        <Field>
          <Name>Ask Price</Name>
          <Type>Price (4)</Type>
          <Size>10</Size>
          <Description>The price on the ask with 6 whole number places followed by 4 decimal digits. The decimal point is implied by position; it does not appear inside the price field. The price is padded with spaces on the left.</Description>
        </Field>
      </Fields>
    </Message>

  </Messages>

</OmiItchNasdaqEquitiesPdf>
